se„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤because that, when they knew God, they glorified him not as God, neither were thankful; but became vain in their imaginations, and their foolish heart was darkened.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ4Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And changed the glory of the uncorruptible God into an image made like to corruptible man, and to birds, and fourfooted beasts, and creeping things.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Wherefore God also gave them up to uncleanness through the lusts of their own hearts, to dishonour their own bodies between themselves:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…who changed the truth of God into a lie, and worshipped and served the creature more than the Creator, who is blessed for ever. Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆFor this cause God gave them up unto vile affections: for even their women did change the natural use into that which is against nature:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙáand likewise also the men, leaving the natural use of the woman, burned in their lust one toward another; men with men working that which is unseemly, and receiving in themselves that recompence of their error which was meet.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”And even as they did not like to retain God in their knowledge, God gave them over to a reprobate mind, to do those things which are not convenient;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™being filled with all unrighteousness, fornication, wickedness, covetousness, maliciousness; full of envy, murder, debate, deceit, malignity; whisperers,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙibackbiters, haters of God, despiteful, proud, boasters, inventors of evil things, disobedient to parents,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[without understanding, covenantbreakers, without natural affection, implacable, unmerciful:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–who knowing the judgment of God, that they which commit such things are worthy of death, not only do the same, but have pleasure in them that do them.¦layout ªlast_verse 